;; C++'s dg check's divergences (doc/cpp/CPP-SURVEY.md, "As built: CX9 (write-ahead)"; bin/repr-cpp dg): the classes every
;; file of g++.dg's dg-error and preprocess parts that does not pass falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A
;; file's class is the first whose :match finds "RESULT REASON" as test/cpp/check-dg-linux-amd64.edn (and
;; test/repr/cpp/dg-preprocess-results.edn) write them: "fail KIND: DETAIL", KIND one of missed (an expected error line
;; without an error; "missed: accepted; ..." when the oracle accepted the unit), extra (an error on a line that expects
;; none), both, stopped (errors outside the main file, or the expected lines after a fatal error), refused (repr/cpp's
;; converter refused a unit the oracle accepted), crash and timeout (no class: they fail); the preprocess part's kinds are
;; pp-missed, pp-extra, pp-both, pp-stopped (the shared preprocessor's errors). A failure whose directives g++ 15.2 does not
;; give either carries " [g++: [MISSING EXTRA ...]]" (the recorded reference, test/cpp/ref-dg-gxx15.edn).
;; The dg-error part is the oracle's (CP2 (a), CP3 (a)): repr/cpp has no Sema of its own, the errors are clang 23.1.4's
;; and the expectations g++'s, so the oracle classes are of the design, not gaps of Arbace's code; only refused is a gap
;; of the converter. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :gxx-disagrees
  :title "g++ 15.2 does not give the directives' errors either"
  :kind :design
  :why "the reference, run with the file's options at the file's standard (test/cpp/ref-dg-gxx15.edn), misses an expected line or errs on another: a directive whose selector the targets' tables decide otherwise than DejaGnu on gcc's own build (an effective target taken to hold, test/c/dg-targets.edn), an option the check drops, an xfail DejaGnu counts, a test of another standard than the one the check picks (one of DejaGnu's list, CP210's question): the expectation is not this host's, so the oracle is not judged against it"
  :decided "CX9 (CP11 (a): g++ the reference)"
  :match [#"\[g\+\+: \["]}
 {:id :clang-pedantic
  :title "clang's -pedantic-errors rejects an extension of a later standard that g++ only warns about"
  :kind :design
  :why "g++.dg's default flags are -pedantic-errors -Wno-long-long (dg.exp); clang turns its own extension warnings (C++17 attributes in C++11, a statement in a constexpr function before C++23, invalid UTF-8 in a comment ...) into errors, which g++ gives as pedwarns it does not count or does not give"
  :decided "CX9 (CP2 (a): the oracle's diagnostics)"
  :match [#"^fail (extra|both): .*\[-Werror,-W"]}
 {:id :clang-accepts
  :title "the oracle accepts a unit g++ rejects"
  :kind :design
  :why "a check g++ makes and clang does not (gcc's own pedantic and -fpermissive rules, redeclarations of builtins, gcc's extensions' errors, attributes clang ignores), or one an option enables that the check gives g++ alone (-fconcepts, -fcontracts, -fgnu-tm, -fpermissive, -fmodules-ts ...: clang refuses options it does not know, so they are dropped from its arguments); repr/cpp reads the unit (the converter ran), and the read does not reject what Sema accepted"
  :decided "CX9 (CP2 (a), CP3 (a): the oracle decides acceptance)"
  :match [#"^fail missed: accepted; "]}
 {:id :clang-other-lines
  :title "both reject, the errors on other lines"
  :kind :design
  :why "clang reports the error at another line than g++ (the declaration rather than the use, the template definition rather than its instantiation, the token after a missing one), or recovers otherwise and reports a second error g++ does not, missing one g++ gives"
  :decided "CX9 (CP2 (a): positions are the oracle's)"
  :match [#"^fail both: "]}
 {:id :clang-fewer-errors
  :title "both reject, clang gives errors on fewer of the expected lines"
  :kind :design
  :why "clang stops diagnosing a declaration after its first error, folds several of g++'s errors into one, or gives the rest as notes or warnings; the lines it does give are all expected"
  :decided "CX9 (CP2 (a))"
  :match [#"^fail missed: missed "]}
 {:id :clang-extra
  :title "clang errs on a line that expects no error"
  :kind :design
  :why "clang's stricter checks (a narrowing, a missing typename, an incomplete type, a character too large), an error g++ gives as a warning, or a second error at a line after its recovery; every expected line has an error"
  :decided "CX9 (CP2 (a))"
  :match [#"^fail extra: " #"^fail missed: line 0 expects"]}
 {:id :clang-elsewhere
  :title "clang's errors are located outside the main file"
  :kind :design
  :why "an error in an included header (an instantiation inside libstdc++, a test's own .h) that the file's directives do not place: g++ reports the instantiation's error at the main file's line or under a line-0 directive"
  :decided "CX9 (C's stopped verdict)"
  :match [#"^fail stopped: "]}
 {:id :read-refused
  :title "repr/cpp's converter refuses a unit the oracle accepts"
  :kind :gap
  :why "a construct the converter has no form for in a macro (CP79 (b)'s refusals) or a gap it reports (:cpp/gap): the read level's open cases (CX4-CX5's classes, test/repr/cpp/roundtrip-known.edn)"
  :decided "CX9; CX5"
  :match [#"^fail refused: "]}
 {:id :pp-diag
  :title "the shared preprocessor does not give cpplib's diagnostic"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "cpplib's checks the port (arbace.repr.c.pp in C++ mode, CX2) does not make: identifiers' UCNs and UTF-8 that are invalid or not in NFC (-Winvalid-utf8, normalize), #elifdef and #warning before C++23 under -pedantic-errors, extra tokens after #endif, the module directives' macro rules (cpp-7 .. cpp-20), a #line number with digit separators, the 'began here' note gcc gives as an error"
  :decided "CX9; CX2 (pp-check judges the tokens, not the diagnostics)"
  :match [#"^fail pp-(missed|both|stopped): "]}
 {:id :pp-extra
  :title "the shared preprocessor errs where cpplib does not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "an #error or a __has_include answer of a header the host data does not hold, a diagnostic the port gives as an error that cpplib gives as a warning"
  :decided "CX9; CX2"
  :match [#"^fail pp-extra: "]}
]
